{#-
Derives a visual anchor: the short, fixed keyword list that gets injected verbatim
into every image prompt featuring this subject.

Called once per subject and cached (Character.visual_anchor / Scene.visual_anchor),
because deriving appearance fresh on each generation is what made every image show a
different person. See docs/fork/visual-consistency-design.md.

Modes, set via `anchor_mode`:
  - "character": vars = character
  - "scene": vars = scene

Extractors:
  - anchor: AnchorExtractor("<ANCHOR>", "</ANCHOR>")
-#}
<|SECTION:SOURCE MATERIAL|>
{% if anchor_mode == "character" %}
Subject: {{ character.name }}
{% if character.base_attributes.get("species") %}Species: {{ character.base_attributes.get("species") }}{% endif %}
{% if character.base_attributes.get("gender") %}Gender: {{ character.base_attributes.get("gender") }}{% endif %}
{% if character.base_attributes.get("age") %}Age: {{ character.base_attributes.get("age") }}{% endif %}

{% if character.base_attributes.get("appearance") %}
Appearance:
{{ character.base_attributes.get("appearance") }}
{% else %}
No appearance attribute exists. Work from the description below, and extract only what
it actually states about how the subject looks.

Description:
{{ character.description }}
{% endif %}
{% elif anchor_mode == "wardrobe" %}
Subject: {{ character.name }}

What the story currently reports about their clothing and condition:
{{ wardrobe_report }}
{% else %}
Setting: {{ scene.title or scene.name }}
Genre context: {{ scene.context }}
{% if location %}Current location: {{ location }}{% endif %}

Premise:
{{ scene.description }}
{% endif %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>

<|SECTION:TASK|>
{% if anchor_mode == "character" %}
Extract a compact, comma-delimited keyword list describing what {{ character.name }}
physically looks like. This list is reused unchanged in every image of them, so it must
describe only what is permanently true of their appearance.

Include, where the source material states it: species or race, skin colour and
markings, hair colour and how it is worn, eye colour or notable eye features, build and
height, and distinctive anatomy.

**Exclude clothing entirely** - no garments, uniforms, armour, footwear, belts or
accessories. What someone wears changes between scenes; this list does not. Clothing is
supplied separately, per image, and a garment named here would contradict it.

Target 5 to 8 keywords. The whole prompt must fit one 77-token chunk, and this
is only one part of it - prefer the traits that make them recognisable over completeness.
{% elif anchor_mode == "wardrobe" %}
Extract a compact, comma-delimited keyword list describing what {{ character.name }} is
wearing right now, and any visible physical condition they are in.

Include, where the source material states it: garments and their colour and fit,
footwear or the lack of it, armour, visible equipment, and visible condition - dirt,
blood, injuries, soaked clothing, dishevelment.

**Exclude their permanent appearance** - no species, skin colour, hair, eyes, build or
anatomy. Those are supplied separately and would be duplicated here.

If the source material says they are undressed, say so plainly and list nothing else.

Target 3 to 6 keywords.
{% else %}
Extract a compact, comma-delimited keyword list describing where this story takes
place. This list is reused unchanged in every image of the scene, so it must describe
only what is permanently true of the setting.

Include: the concrete location type, the genre, the dominant materials or architecture,
and the dominant colour or lighting palette.

Target 4 to 6 keywords. The whole prompt must fit one 77-token chunk. Name the place
and its genre; do not inventory its contents.
{% endif %}

Rules:

1. **Only physically visible things.** A diffusion model can render violet skin. It
   cannot render competence, grief, duty, or a classified archive.
2. **No personality, no history, no plot.** Nothing about what the subject wants,
   fears, remembers{{ ", or is doing right now" if anchor_mode != "wardrobe" else "" }}.
3. **No camera or format language.** No orientation, framing, shot type, composition,
   or aspect ratio. Those are set elsewhere.
4. **No art style.** No medium, no rendering style, no quality tags. Those are set
   elsewhere.
5. **No proper names.** An image model has never heard of {{ "this character" if anchor_mode == "character" else "this ship or place" }}.
   Describe the thing, do not name it.
6. **Invent nothing.** If the source material does not state a trait, leave it out.

Output the keyword list between <ANCHOR></ANCHOR> tags, on one line, comma-delimited.
{% if anchor_mode == "character" %}
Example shape (do not copy the content): <ANCHOR>alien woman, deep violet skin, geometric facial markings, indigo hair pulled back, large black eyes, lean and tall, four-fingered hands</ANCHOR>
{% elif anchor_mode == "wardrobe" %}
Example shape (do not copy the content): <ANCHOR>fitted dark blue-grey utility suit, tool loops on belt, bare feet, smudged with soot</ANCHOR>
{% else %}
Example shape (do not copy the content): <ANCHOR>starship interior, deep space, science fiction, worn metal panelling, exposed conduits, cool blue screen glow</ANCHOR>
{% endif %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% if llm_can_be_coerced() %}{{ set_prepared_response("<ANCHOR>") }}{% endif %}
